<reference id="kitControl-Nand" xml:lang="en-us" class="- topic/topic       reference/reference "><title class="- topic/title ">kitControl-Nand</title><shortdesc class="- topic/shortdesc ">This component takes two to four Boolean inputs and returns <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">false</systemoutput> only if all inputs are <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">true</systemoutput>.</shortdesc><prolog class="- topic/prolog "><author translate="no" type="creator" class="- topic/author ">Claudia Serwe &lt;claudia.serwe@tridium.com&gt;</author><metadata class="- topic/metadata "><keywords class="- topic/keywords "/></metadata></prolog><refbody class="- topic/body        reference/refbody "><section class="- topic/section ">
    
    <p class="- topic/p "><image placement="break" width="500" href="../graphic/kitControl-Nand.png" class="- topic/image "/></p><p class="- topic/p ">The Nand operator is only <option class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/option ">false</option> if all of its inputs are <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">true</systemoutput>. If one of its inputs is <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">false</systemoutput>, it returns  <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">true</systemoutput></p><p class="- topic/p "><image placement="break" width="500" href="../graphic/kitControl-Nand2.png" class="- topic/image "/></p><p class="- topic/p "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Nand</uicontrol> is available in the <uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Logic</uicontrol> folder
of the <apiname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/apiname ">kitControl</apiname></p>
    </section></refbody></reference>